Delivery Page — Add Credit Popup Enhancement (Detailed)

Goal:
Enhance the “Add Credit” popup on the Delivery page by introducing an Area selector and a customer name input with a filtered customer dropdown.

Requirements:
1) Add Area field (first in the popup)
   - Label: “Area”
   - Control: <select>
   - Options: Loaded from saved Area Listing data.
   - Must load dynamically from the same storage used by Area Listing.

2) Customer Name field (after Area)
   - Label: “Customer Name”
   - Control: text input, user can type freely.
   - As the user types, show a dropdown list of customer names.

3) Filtered Customer Dropdown
   - Source: Customer Listing data.
   - Filter: Only customers whose “Area” matches the selected Area.
   - If no area is selected, show no results or a “Select Area first” hint.
   - Selecting a customer from the dropdown fills the Customer Name input.

4) Behavior
   - Changing the Area resets the Customer Name input and dropdown list.
   - Preserve existing credit popup styling and validation patterns.
   - Do not break existing credit calculations or save flow.

Implementation notes:
- Follow existing modal/component patterns in delivery.js.
- Keep storage API consistent with existing listing pages.
- Use the same DOM structure/classes used for other popup inputs for visual consistency.

Acceptance:
- Area appears at the top.
- Customer dropdown only shows customers in the chosen area.
- Selected customer fills the name input.
- Save works normally and stores the customer name as before.
